    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 run / 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature so `POST /api/owners` records, and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns, the number of existing owners that shared the same first and last name (case-insensitively) *before* this owner was created.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes the count just before saving via a new `namesakeCount(firstName, lastName)` helper that counts existing owners matching on normalized (trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased) first + last name, reusing the same `normalizeName` used by the household check.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`, `Integer` so pre-existing rows with a NULL column load cleanly) plus getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe test creates two owners sharing `firstName`+`lastName` (distinct addresses, so no household 409), and asserts the second owner's `namesakeCount == 1`. It passes, as does the full suite.",
